   "evidence": "Rank.lean:60-63 extracts `i.hom.w` and applies `Scheme.Hom.finrank_comp_left_of_isIso`; Mathlib's FlatRank.lean:145 has only the `f \u226b g` form, and the repo's only iso-transport helpers are property-level (`MorphismProperty.over_iso_iff` at CartierDuality/FiniteLocallyFree.lean:91-96, FiniteType.lean:90).",
   "file": "TauCeti/AlgebraicGeometry/AffineGroupScheme/CartierDuality/Rank.lean",
   "fix": "Add a public lemma for the general step \u2014 e.g. `theorem finrank_eq_of_iso {S : Scheme} {X Y : Over S} (e : X \u2245 Y) [Flat Y.hom] [IsFinite Y.hom] : X.hom.finrank = Y.hom.finrank := by rw [\u2190 e.hom.w, Scheme.Hom.finrank_comp_left_of_isIso]` (statement is Mathlib-only, so its home is a general `Scheme.Hom.finrank` file, not this proof) \u2014 plus, if convenient, the bundled-category corollary for `e : G \u2245 H` in `FiniteLocallyFreeCommAffineGroupSchemeCat`, and use it to shorten lines 51-64.",
   "issue": "The transport of `finrank` along an isomorphism over the base is built inline (lines 51-63: `F.mapIso`, `i.hom.w`, `Scheme.Hom.finrank_comp_left_of_isIso`) and never exposed. `finrank_cartierDual` only speaks about the specific object `cartierDual R G`, so the consumer named in the PR description (Layer 2E, transporting the kernel rank through `ker \u03c6\u0302 \u2245 (ker \u03c6)\u1d30`) has an isomorphism, not an equality, and must reconstruct this 12-line dance; Mathlib offers nothing for it (`grep '\\bOver\\b' mathlib/Mathlib/AlgebraicGeometry/Morphisms/FlatRank.lean` \u2192 no matches).",
   "line": "44"
  }
 ],
